<title>USA: Simpson registered on quality standards.</title>
<headline>Simpson registered on quality standards.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH, Mich. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Simpson Industries Inc on Thursday said it reached its goal of attaining QS-9000 registration at all of its facilities by the end of 1996.</p>
<p>QS-9000 is the name for the supplier quality standards established by Chrysler Corp, Ford Motor Co and General Motors Corp, covering manufacturing and business processes.</p>
<p>Simpson provides powertrain and chassis products to original equipment manufacturers in automotive and diesel engine markets.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
